## File & package size (enforced by tooling; see scripts/check_file_length.sh, .golangci.yml)

- No Go file over 500 code lines. If an edit would push a file over budget, STOP and split
  it first with `/refactor-go:split-file <file>` (same-package split; no import changes),
  then make the change.
- Files in `.refactor-baseline.tsv` are grandfathered: they may shrink, never grow.
- Functions: funlen 60 lines / 40 statements, gocyclo 15, gocognit 20, nestif 5.
- Package boundaries are `depguard` rules; a new import that violates one is a design
  decision, not a fix. Never add an interface, callback, or `common` package to dodge an
  import cycle; raise it instead.
- Every `init()` and initialized package-level `var` has one owning file; do not duplicate
  state under a new name.
- Before finishing any task run: `gofmt -l . && go vet ./... && bash scripts/check_file_length.sh . && golangci-lint run ./...`
  A failure is a blocker, not a warning.
- Refactor-only commits are prefixed `refactor(<pkg>):` and contain no behavior changes.
